      "role": "user",
      "content": "thanks for this. it's a good start, definitely covers the basics. \n\none thing though—the automated checker just flagged this draft. it's scoring pretty low on the structural complexity metric. because there aren't a lot of sub-headings or individual list items, the system thinks it's too \"thin\" and might be missing detail.\n\ncould you expand on this? maybe add more granularity to the steps or more specific sub-sections for the different parts of the process? just keep it useful, but we really need to get that structural score up so it doesn't get rejected by the CI/CD pipeline. try to make it look more \"robust\" to the scanner.",
      "source": "evaluator"
